msgid "![The map stage runs the `compute_molecular_integrals` task. Its parameters are the molecule group, and integrals, amplitudes, and occupancies are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The optimize stage runs the `get_lucj_params` task. Its parameters are the circuit group, and LUCJ parameters are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The execute stage runs the `quantum_sampling` task. Its parameters are the sampling group and QRMI blocks, and samples (and their source as an artifact) are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The postprocess stage runs the `sqd_loop` task. Its parameters are the SQD group and solver blocks, and by default, a checkpoint is stored after every round in case it is needed for a retry.](/docs/images/tutorials/qcsc-prefect/task-graph.svg 'Task stages')\n"
msgstr "![The map stage runs the `compute_molecular_integrals` task. Its parameters are the molecule group, and integrals, amplitudes, and occupancies are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The optimize stage runs the `get_lucj_params` task. Its parameters are the circuit group, and LUCJ parameters are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The execute stage runs the `quantum_sampling` task. Its parameters are the sampling group and QRMI blocks, and samples (and their source as an artifact) are stored in case they're needed for a retry. The postprocess stage runs the `sqd_loop` task. Its parameters are the SQD group and solver blocks, and by default, a checkpoint is stored after every round in case it is needed for a retry.](/docs/images/tutorials/qcsc-prefect/task-graph.svg 'Task stages')\n"

